---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavierStokesProofAtlas from "@/components/labs/NavierStokesProofAtlas.astro";
import { physicsStorySteps } from "@/components/labs/navierStokesPhysics";
import { radialProgressSummary } from "@/components/labs/navierStokesProgress";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Navier–Stokes proof atlas — bordumb"
  description="An interactive map of the sparse Gaussian certificate, its ranked proof ledger, the active radial-tail decomposition, and the remaining logical distance to the Clay problem."
>
  <article class="atlas-page page-shell">
    <header class="atlas-hero">
      <div class="hero-index" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>NS</span>
        <i></i>
        <small>2026·08·02</small>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Navier–Stokes · formal proof observatory</p>
        <h1>One obstruction,<br /><em>under a microscope.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-deck">
          The project is testing whether one tempting shortcut for controlling
          three-dimensional fluid spin can work. Its explicit Gaussian witness
          may rule out that shortcut. This atlas keeps the physical story, the
          exact Lean proof, and the remaining distance to Clay visibly separate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-boundary">
        <span>Current boundary</span>
        <strong>Angular coefficient j=2</strong>
        <p>
          Two of five angular coefficients are kernel-checked. The middle
          coefficient is written and currently replaying through the definitive
          persistent Lake target.
        </p>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Evidence</dt>
            <dd>{radialProgressSummary.label}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Conclusion</dt>
            <dd>Closure obstruction only</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="audience-gateway" aria-labelledby="audience-gateway-title">
      <div class="gateway-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">New to the mathematics? Start here.</p>
        <h2 id="audience-gateway-title">Follow one idea from water to proof.</h2>
        <p>
          Begin with moving specks and spinning paddle wheels. Each stop adds
          one necessary idea; the equations and theorem details remain beside
          the physical explanation for expert readers.
        </p>
        <a href="/labs/navier-stokes/flow-and-spin/">
          Begin with flow and spin <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <ol>
        {physicsStorySteps.map((step) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/labs/navier-stokes/${step.id}/`}>
              <span>{step.index}</span>
              <strong>{step.label}</strong>
              <small>{step.summary}</small>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Already fluent in PDE or Lean?</p>
        <strong>The research atlas begins below.</strong>
        <p>
          The workflow, ranked commits, exact certificate anatomy, and logical
          distance to Clay are preserved in full.
        </p>
        <a href="#proof-atlas">Jump to the formal work ↓</a>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <NavierStokesProofAtlas />

    <section class="reading-note" aria-labelledby="reading-note-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How to read the atlas</p>
        <h2 id="reading-note-title">A child theorem does not solve its parent.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-columns">
        <p>
          <strong>Kernel-checked</strong> means Lean accepted the theorem and
          its reported dependencies contain only the standard foundational
          axioms used throughout Mathlib. It does not mean every theorem that
          imports it is complete.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Exact certificate</strong> means rational computation found
          a finite proof object without floating-point theorem data. It becomes
          a formal theorem only after Lean independently checks its generated
          inequalities and the assembly covers the stated domain.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Closure obstruction</strong> means the proposed universal
          estimate cannot hold in its current form. Eliminating that strategy
          narrows the search; it supplies neither a global regularity estimate
          nor a finite-time singular solution.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="atlas-footer">
      <p>
        The companion visual study explains the vorticity geometry that
        motivated the formal program before the Gaussian obstruction emerged.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/labs/vortex-stretching">
        Explore the vortex geometry
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .atlas-page {
    padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
  }

  .atlas-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(17rem, 0.38fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .hero-index {
    display: grid;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 15rem;
    justify-items: center;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .hero-index span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .hero-index i {
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 8rem;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .hero-index small {
    align-self: end;
    font-size: 0.52rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(3.25rem, 7.5vw, 7rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.063em;
    line-height: 0.88;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .hero-deck {
    max-width: 43rem;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.8vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.58;
  }

  .hero-boundary {
    padding: 1.25rem 0 0 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hero-boundary > span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero-boundary > strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .hero-boundary > p {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .hero-boundary dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-boundary dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-block: 0.55rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .hero-boundary dt {
    color: var(--faint);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero-boundary dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .audience-gateway {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(14rem, 0.36fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }

  .gateway-intro h2 {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .gateway-intro > p:last-of-type,
  .audience-gateway aside p:last-of-type {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .gateway-intro > a,
  .audience-gateway aside a {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.3rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .audience-gateway ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .audience-gateway li {
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .audience-gateway li a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .audience-gateway li span,
  .audience-gateway li small {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.56rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .audience-gateway li strong {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .audience-gateway li a:hover strong,
  .audience-gateway li a:focus-visible strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .audience-gateway aside {
    padding: 1.25rem 0 0 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .audience-gateway aside > strong {
    display: block;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .reading-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }

  .reading-note h2 {
    max-width: 25rem;
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .reading-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .reading-columns p {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .reading-columns strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .atlas-footer {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .atlas-footer p {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .atlas-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .hero-boundary {
      grid-column: 2;
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .reading-note {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .audience-gateway {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .audience-gateway aside {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      padding-left: 0;
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .atlas-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-index {
      display: none;
    }

    .hero-boundary {
      grid-column: 1;
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    .reading-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .audience-gateway {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .audience-gateway ol {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .atlas-footer {
      display: grid;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
